<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Angle in a semicircle</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>\(A\), \(B\) and \(C\) are points on a circle with centre \(O\). \(AB\) is a diameter of the circle. The angle \(CAB = {@ang@}^\circ\).</p>
<p>{@img@}</p>

<p><strong>(a)</strong> Find the angle \(ACB\).</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] degrees [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p><strong>(b)</strong> Find the angle \(ABC\).</p>
<p>[[input:ans2]] degrees [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>

<p><strong>(a)</strong> The angle in a semicircle is a right angle. Since \(AB\) is a diameter, the angle at \(C\) is:</p>
\[ ACB = 90^\circ \]

<p><strong>(b)</strong> The angles in triangle \(ABC\) add up to \(180^\circ\).</p>
\[ ABC = 180^\circ - 90^\circ - {@ang@}^\circ = {@third@}^\circ \]]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
